# MUL, DIV and the integer instructions on 32-bit values. Observed: products
# and quotients are formed in 64 bits and wrap to 32; MUL rounds half away
# from zero, DIV truncates; ADD, SUB, NEG, ABS, FLOOR and CEILING wrap; the
# comparisons are signed. The values depend on the integer width: on 64-bit
# targets the reference keeps what wraps on 32-bit ARMv7, whose results this
# probe's record holds.
# Each glyph's program computes values and writes value i into the y of
# point i of a 32-point contour (SCFS along y), so the dump shows them.
heights 16384
wraps-at-32-bits
fpgm
  PUSH 0; FDEF; ENDF
end
glyph advance 400
  contour 0 0, 10 0, 20 0, 30 0, 40 0, 50 0, 60 0, 70 0, 80 0, 90 0, 100 0, 110 0, 120 0, 130 0, 140 0, 150 0, 160 0, 170 0, 180 0, 190 0, 200 0, 210 0, 220 0, 230 0, 240 0, 250 0, 260 0, 270 0, 280 0, 290 0, 300 0, 310 0
